Subject: [PATCH v11 3/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Relay mail to Fastmail with
 smtprelay
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: nplnvkkrlsomxnuwxrupuklwsxvyqrmk

Agents need to send mail without the credentials, and to learn at
once whether a message was accepted. A queuing MTA answers before
Fastmail has seen the message, so a rejection comes back later as a
bounce nobody reads. smtprelay relays each message during the
client's session and hands back Fastmail's answer, so every failure
reaches the sender as an SMTP reply.

The sender and recipient allowlists stop a mistaken address before
it leaves beastie. The Fastmail login reaches smtprelay only through
its environment, built from mail-creds at start, so no config file
carries it. smtprelay takes the login as part of a URL, where an
"@", ":", "/" or "#" in the password would end the field early, so
jq percent-encodes the login and password on the way in and any app
password works.

If mail-creds lacks the login or the password, smtprelay refuses to
start and names the file. Otherwise the fault would surface only at
the first send, as a Fastmail login failure handed to whichever agent
happened to send first.

remotes.env runs from rc(8), whose PATH at boot leaves out
/usr/local/bin, so it names jq in full. The README describes the path
a message takes from a client through smtprelay to Fastmail.
